  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Kosovo Adapt Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kosovo):  .This new activity will increase public and private sector.awareness and demand for government initiatives, including new smart incentives.and innovations, so that Kosovo will become more resilient and improve its.ability to address environmental challenges. These challenges.disproportionately affect the poorest and most vulnerable and will make.reducing unemployment and improving the economy significantly more difficult..Economic-growth strategies and policies must find ways to reduce, mitigate, and.compensate for the impacts of environmental degradation and risk. Addressing.these risks through the adoption of strong environmental safeguards,.particularly policies and smart technologies that will mitigate the negative.effects of environmental harm, will spur innovation and the adoption of.sustainable practices. While these issues are global, they are felt on a local.scale. Smart technologies refer to products or services that improve.operational performance while also reducing costs, energy consumption, waste,.or negative effects on the environment. The goal of these technologies is to protect.the environment, repair past damage, and conserve natural resources. The types.of smart technologies that may be introduced and adopted by the activity could.include water-saving technologies (drip irrigation systems), anti-hail nets,.noise pollution technologies, environmentally friendly construction materials,.etc. The activity aligns with ICS Objectives 1.3 and 3.2 by strengthening.Kosovo&apos;s commitment to its ambitious climate change and environmental.protection agenda, which also ensures Kosovo&apos;s readiness for EU accession. The.activity also aligns with CAATSA Goal 8 supporting economic resilience (20% of.funding) through technical assistance in supporting economic resilience through.climate change awareness raising and new climate smart initiatives... ...</narrative>
  </description>
